==Strategy==
This stage is similar to [[Ogre Island (Deadly)|Ogre Island]] and [[Fish Hell (Insane)|Fish Hell]], with a stronger Super Metal Hippoe rather than a Berserkory, and with Li'l Islands being even tankier than Manic Islands, albeit with only barely higher damage than Crazed Fish and with a longer attack cycle. Because of this, a similar strategy can be used, however this would be difficult due to the unit restrictions, though is arguably even easier otherwise since there is no heavy pressure from Berserkory. [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] retains her usefulness from Ogre Island, as when stacked she has massive amounts of DPS that can shred through the Li'l Island Cats.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]]: Like in the other Fish variant stages, her spammability will allow her to rack up DPS over time.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]]: Similar to [[Ogre Island (Deadly)|Ogre Island]], Bahamut can be used to dish out an occasional high damage attack to cripple or outright kill the Li'l Islands. Don't use the True Form, as he'll simply rush in and die.
*[[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]]: With its spammability and resistance against Traitless enemies, it is absolutely powerful when it comes to stalling the Li'l Islands.
*[[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Space Marine Cat]]: Just like in Fish Hell, it's a reliable critter for the Super Metal Hippoe, though at this point Catasaurus would be a more reliable pick thanks to its higher damage and Crit talents, though it has higher range to not be beaten by the Islands.
*[[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]]: A reliable critter for the Super Metal Hippoe, with high damage, greater spammability compared to Space Marine, though the lower range leaves it more vulnerable to the Islands. It is highly recommended to get the Crit talent, as it increases its crit chance from 7% to 12%.
*[[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]]: The Li'l Island Cats outrange her by 10. However, with her Critical Hit Talent, and some luck, she can defeat the Super Metal Hippoe in one to two Crits (depending on her level). She also serves as a pseudo-meatshield.
*[[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando Jr.]]: To put it in simple terms he does absolute wonders here, he can devastate the hordes of islands that come out with his surge. Keep in mind as long as you keep Super Metal Hippoe alive you can using him as a stepping stool for his surges.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]]: Their effectively limitless HP allows them to fill in the gaps when other meatshields die, and their Immunity to [[Knockback]] comes in handy against Super Metal Hippoe. However, they are not without their weaknesses: if spammed carelessly, they may drain your already strained wallet.

